The actual problem is in the error path: if the first sysfs_create_link succeeds but the second one fails, the function removes the "typec" link and returns, leaving the port->usb2_dev still set. Later when typec_partner_unlink_device tries to remove that link during unregister, it gets ENOENT because the link was already removed during the failed creation, and this error isn't propagated properly. The fix involves ensuring link_device failures are handled correctly so unlink doesn't attempt to remove links that were never successfully created.
